  "description": "Does a witness name a producer that EXISTS, under ANY spelling? Decides by VALUE (does a field hold a .py path that resolves in the tree) rather than by KEY NAME, because the fields are polymorphic: `computation` is present on ~91% of witnesses and holds the witness ID, not a script, on almost all of them; `source` usually holds a literature PDF but sometimes a .py. Three prior orphan counts each keyed on one field (qou-tekx scriptFile, qou-bake computation, qou-agvb producer) and each OVER-reported orphans by calling provenanced witnesses unprovenanced. Does NOT check that the named script actually writes the witness -- that is witness_provenance_audit.py, which needs a scriptFile to start from and cannot see the witnesses this audit finds.",
